WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:04.352
This slide compares a vague query with a context-aware version.

00:00:04.352 --> 00:00:08.097
The vague query says, 'Can I still do it late?' On its own,

00:00:08.097 --> 00:00:12.797
almost any policy about deadlines could look relevant.

00:00:12.797 --> 00:00:19.662
The context-aware version asks whether a student can request a payment plan after the tuition due date.

00:00:19.662 --> 00:00:27.017
Now the important concepts are explicit: payment plan, request, tuition due date, and lateness.

00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:29.342
[tts-break] Run both searches and compare the rankings.

00:00:29.342 --> 00:00:37.842
This is a useful demonstration because it shows that retrieval quality is partly a query-understanding

00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:43.507
problem. The embedding model cannot use context that we never provide.

00:00:43.507 --> 00:00:49.307
In a chat application, the retrieval query may need to be constructed from the current message plus relevant

00:00:49.307 --> 00:00:56.873
conversation history. The final answer can still respond naturally to the user's original question.
